1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
So, Clawdbot / OpenClaw and Peter have single-handedly taken the open source community...

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:13,000
...forward into the future by six months or more in less than six weeks. Yep, there I said it.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:20,000
I think despite the moltbook(.com) fiasco and the AI slop all over the place...

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
...I think Clawdbot is a net positive for the community.

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Because everything seems to have happened in the open...

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
...and because there is so much transparency in the way everybody is approaching building and publishing.

7
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:43,000
And I'm glad to see that a lot of the community members, despite not necessarily being on the side of Clawdbot...

8
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:49,000
...have been kind and gracious enough to be a lovely safety net and exposed the vulnerabilities that have sort of surfaced.

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:55,000
I think it's good. As Mark Zuckerberg famously said, "Move fast and break things."

10
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,000
And I think in this case, the downside is negligible in comparison to what everybody's learned.

11
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:06,000
I maintain that there are more people now in the fold. Folks who had no idea about this...

12
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:11,000
...are now entering the circle, and those on the fringes have become much more active.

13
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:17,000
And the overall open source community has benefited significantly...

14
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,000
...thanks to all the PR and noise around Clawdbot and... Peter.

15
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Of course, the one key thing that I want to highlight is it's also given a whole bunch of people...

16
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:32,000
...an amazing preview of what agentic AI truly can do.

17
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:39,000
So yeah, I really hope more people keep building. I hope they are not discouraged by some of the issues...

18
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:47,000
...and faux pas that have been exposed, but continue to learn from it and just keep shipping
